  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "4.0.0 (packaging): the shared contracts assembly (FoxTS.Ecm.Sdk.Contracts) is now BUNDLED inside this package instead of being shipped as a separate NuGet package. There is a single package to install. The contract types and their FoxTS.Ecm.Sdk.Contracts.* namespaces are unchanged, so source code does not need to change — but if you previously referenced the FoxTS.Ecm.Sdk.Contracts package explicitly (e.g. a transitive pin), remove that reference. No public API changes vs 3.0.0.\n\n3.0.0 (breaking): redesigned client surface. New IEcmClient facade with resource clients (Documents, Tags, TagManagement, Acl, Lookups, TaggingRules, Outbox). Document API is document-id-centric: DownloadAsync(documentId, versionId?), GetViewerUrl, and GetDownloadUrlAsync (server-issued presigned URL) replace the removed version-keyed download/delete/url methods. Tags split by actor: Tags (user self-service, namespace optional - defaults to your personal namespace) vs TagManagement (admin, explicit namespace required, plus namespace CRUD). New ILookupClient (GetDocumentTypesAsync, ResolveUserAsync). IEcmUserContext is now async (GetUserKeyAsync). Multi-targets net8.0 and net10.0. AddEcmSdkClients() enables deferred/hot-reload configuration. Typed DocumentPermission ACL accessors (GetPermissions).",
